4</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>208</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15175614</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ajic.2003.10.013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Paulus</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>van Saene</surname><given-names>HK</given-names></name><name><surname>Hemsworth</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hughes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Pizer</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A prospective study of septicaemia on a paediatric oncology unit: a three-year experience at The Royal Liverpool Children's Hospital, Alder Hey, UK</article-title><source>Eur J Cancer</source><year>2005</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>2132</fpage><lpage>2140</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16129600</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ejca.2005.04.037</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Laws</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobbe</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Dilloo</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dettenkofer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Meisel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Geisel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Haas</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gobel</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulze-Robbecke</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Surveillance of nosocomial infections in paediatric recipients of bone marrow or peripheral blood stem cell transplantation during neutropenia, compared with adult recipients</article-t